      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>It's not just \"disorientation\" though. It feels deeper than that. Like I’ve seen something everyone else is too blind to see. I look at them—the people working their 9-5s, worrying about stupid stuff—and I feel like I’m from a different species. There's this massive gap between what I know the world is really like and the \"fake\" way they all live. It’s exhausting pretending to be one of them.",
